  "body": "P0: the lathe post accepted a turning op whose fitted spindle leans in Y and cut a taper error (#62).\n\n**What changed**\n- New `crates/app/src/operation/spindle_law.rs`, called from `collect_job` (validate early): every turning op, and Drill on a plain lathe, is refused by name when its fitted axis is not world Z through the work-offset origin. The origin comes from `posting::wcs_context`, the same function that gives the post its origin, so generation and post read one spindle.\n- Tolerance: the axis may stand at most 0.0005 mm (radius) from the work-offset Z line at both the part's lowest and highest Z - half the posted diameter's last digit, so a passing part posts the same digits as a perfectly placed one. (An angle limit of 0.01 deg was dropped: over 100 mm it allows ~17 um of radius drift.)\n- The message names the lean in degrees, the offset in mm at mid-height and the work-offset slot, and says to align the part's axis with world Z and move the work offset onto it.\n- Parts the fit cannot read as revolved, or whose axis lies within 1 deg of the table, pass to the turning code's existing refusals unchanged.\n- No post-side check: the post only sees points, and a part leaning in Y looks like a plumb one move by move; catching it there would need a new parameter in every lathe stream (every golden changes). The post's existing both-X-and-Y refusal stays.\n- Valid programs post byte-identically; lathe goldens unchanged.\n\n**Pinned by** `lathe_spindle_law::{a_bar_leaning_in_y_on_the_origin_is_refused_by_name_at_generation (written first - it posted a taper: X-1.708 diameters with drifting Z), a_plumb_bar_off_the_work_origin_is_refused_by_name_at_generation, an_axial_drill_on_a_bar_off_the_work_origin_is_refused_by_name, a_plumb_bar_on_the_origin_or_under_a_moved_work_offset_posts_the_same_program}`.\n\n**Gates**: quick gate green against origin/main (app + ui suites, 11.7 min); camcraft-ui lib 198 passed; the agent ran 19 app binaries one by one (turning*, lathe_post*, posting, conformance, drilling_axial, ...) and clippy -D warnings - all green.\n\nPR #60 (#19, lathe field sim) depends on this guarantee: it revolves about the fitted axis, which this makes the machine spindle. Merge this first.\n\nChangelog: fix(app): turning ops (and the lathe axial drill) whose fitted axis is not world Z through the work offset within 0.0005 mm are refused by name at generation instead of posting a taper or eccentric\n\nFixes #62\n",
